A||||4||martin1875||exhaust mainfolds||||1||
Z||000000||martin1875||01-26-2001||11:43 PM||||i want to port my stock exhaust mainfolds. i have the exhaust system off right now due to a hole in my cat, so the access to the front maifold will be easier. now to my question. i need to know what gaskets you recomend and where to get them. can i get grade 8 or stainless bolts to replace the old ones. thanks for the help.||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||01-27-2001||12:44 AM||||Go to Auto Zone or wherever and get Fel-Pro brand gaskets for a '93 Camaro 3.4.  They look different from the Fiero gaskets, but they work just fine and cost 1/4 the price of Fiero gaskets ($6 vs. $23).<P>Fel-Pro part #90864 <P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||01-27-2001||08:28 AM||||Take one of the bolts to like a NAPA store and have the threads matched up. they have different grades and stainless. Also could try a local speed shop. Instead of bolts, id use studs with nuts instead. Also recommend the felpro. Most of turbo suppliers recommend them because they will stand up to more pressure than stock ones.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mark||01-27-2001||09:24 AM||||First, I would NOT use the Camaro manifold gaskets!!  Yes, the Fiero gaskets cost about 4x as much, but they are designed for higher temperature operation.  I used the Fiero gaskets in my car, most people strongly recommend the Fiero gaskets. IMO, it's just not worth the risk of going through all that work again (should the cheap gasket fail) for a parts cost savings of about $17.<P>Secondly, the exhaust manifold bolts are M8 x 1.25 thread.  Three of the front bolts are studs, the others (front and back) are bolts. I could not find these in SS or Grade 8 (Grade 8 is an SAE rating, by the way, and is not applicable to metric hardware)  Metric studs with the right ammount of thread on each side are tuff to find.  I had to make my studs by cutting the heads off of same fully-threaded bolts (3 bolts = three hacksaw blades!).  Pep-Boys is a good source for metric hardware.<P><p>[This message has been edited by Mark (edited 01-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||StuGood||01-27-2001||09:57 AM||||Raydar, some time back, mentioned using some Saturn parts to use on the forward manifold:<P>GM part number 21006951 Saturn intake manifold stud.<P>GM part number 11502609 flange nut.<P>Alternate:<BR>Au-ve-co Products P/N 18514 + P/N 11644.<P>Anyway, the idea is, use the studs in lieu of the original bolts, and attach the the heat shields using 2 of the nuts. <P>Apparently, he got the info from Ed Parks.  I'm just quoting Raydar's previous post. Hope this helps  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  ||||reg||3
